From fabd2c0c0fe028b1f32b2b7ebf348823e372797b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Alberto <carlosalberto4ti@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:10:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] staging: media: facetimehd: add driver for Apple FaceTime HD
 (BCM1570) PCIe camera

Add support for the Apple FaceTime HD (Broadcom BCM1570, PCI ID 14e4:1570)
PCIe Image Signal Processor found across Apple MacBook Pro, MacBook Air,
and iMac machines.

Features supported:
- Full V4L2 capture with videobuf2-dma-sg
- Support PipeWire and unaligned USERPTR memfd buffers without stream stalls
- Discrete framesize enumeration (1080p, 720p, VGA, QVGA) and frameintervals
- Lossless hardware digital zoom and sensor cropping (VIDIOC_S_SELECTION)
- Hardware Wide Dynamic Range (HDR / Dynamic Range Compression)
- Auto-Exposure Photometry Metering (Average, Center-Weighted, Spot, Matrix)
- Status / Privacy LED indicator control (V4L2_CID_ILLUMINATORS_1)
- Dynamic power saving profiles (High Performance, Balanced, Low Power)
- Clean-room open-source firmware compatibility (OpenFTHD project)

Link: https://github.com/patjak/facetimehd/pull/368
Original-author: Patrik Jakobsson <patrik.r.jakobsson@gmail.com>
Co-developed-by: Patrik Jakobsson <patrik.r.jakobsson@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Patrik Jakobsson <patrik.r.jakobsson@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Carlos Alberto <carlosalberto4ti@gmail.com>
